I have a general complaint while i am at it ... nethack 3.1.0 has too many
elementary things that applied to older versions more and not enough about its
latest incarnation in the oracle and rumor files ... i have paid a kings ransom
to the oracle and i think i have gotten all of them and there is just not
enough info there ... rumors are very very repetitious when they could be more
varied, and hence more informative (yet still tricky or cleverly disguised).
I really agree the game is impossible to win without spending an unhealthy time
at it or reading spoilers and i dont wish to do either (sigh). Compilers of
future versions, hear my plea re oracle and rumors. Actually it seems new
rumor and oracle files could be written and ported by us without recompiling
nethack.

     those of us who complain loudest are not anti-nethack obviously, or un-
grateful for the _genius_ that goes into a lot of it. ... I think the oracle/
rumor problem is truly at the heart of nethack shortcomings ... players who
would rather go the exhaustive route and spend 50 hrs a week playing nethack
would not have to consult oracles or read fortune cookies if they think that 
is a purer method. Especially on our quests we are simply not given enough
info. And after all, money paid to the oracle could be used for priests instead
so it is not the same as reading spoiler files.

